1
00:00:10,933 --> 00:00:14,000
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,967
[APPLAUSE]

3
00:00:21,967 --> 00:00:28,833
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

4
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:40,400
[MUSIC STOPS]

5
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:42,233
What are you doing?

6
00:00:43,033 --> 00:00:44,900
[SOBBING] It's so heartbreaking.

7
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:46,467
It's so touching.

8
00:00:46,467 --> 00:00:47,967
Didn't you see it?

9
00:00:47,967 --> 00:00:49,633
You're such drama queens!
That part was still funny.

10
00:00:49,633 --> 00:00:51,067
The crying doesn't come
until the end.

11
00:00:51,067 --> 00:00:52,733
You're such drama queens.
You're all so fake!

12
00:00:52,733 --> 00:00:54,200
You probably didn't even watch

13
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:55,867
<i>Call Me Mother</i>  in theaters.
Did you?

14
00:00:55,933 --> 00:00:57,800
- We're just thinking ahead.
- I watched it.

15
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,733
We already knew,
so we started crying early.

16
00:00:59,733 --> 00:01:01,800
But you held
a block screening for it, right?

17
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:02,900
Yeah, because it's funny.

18
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:04,967
<i>Call Me Mother</i>  is number one
on Netflix Philippines.

19
00:01:04,967 --> 00:01:07,333
- True!
- [AUDIENCE CHEERING]

20
00:01:07,367 --> 00:01:08,900
It's such a huge hit.

21
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:10,700
The gay lead was amazing.

22
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:13,233
I heard he even won Best Actor,

23
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:15,000
- so that's why I'm crying.
- Yeah!

24
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,333
That's why I really idolize
that gay guy.

25
00:01:17,333 --> 00:01:19,833
Esnyr's really number one.

26
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:21,500
- Huh?
- Vice, it's you!

27
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:23,833
Me? I'm amazing!
Did you watch it?

28
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:25,733
- Of course!
- What's the story about?

29
00:01:25,733 --> 00:01:27,700
I was with you
when I watched it.

30
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:29,333
- See?
- [VERNA] Oh!

31
00:01:29,333 --> 00:01:31,100
You were behind me
while I was watching.

32
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:32,567
You even sat in front of me?

33
00:01:32,567 --> 00:01:33,700
[LAUGHTER]

34
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:35,400
- That movie's so good!
- It really is, Meme,

35
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:36,933
because I have a crush
on someone in it.

36
00:01:36,933 --> 00:01:38,733
- Who's your crush in the movie?
- That... guy...

37
00:01:38,733 --> 00:01:40,867
- Oh, please!
- I know who your crush is.

38
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:42,167
- Who?
- I know who your crush is.

39
00:01:42,167 --> 00:01:43,900
- Who?
- Is it John Lapuz?

40
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:45,333
[LAUGHTER]

41
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:46,433
- Who?
- No...

42
00:01:46,433 --> 00:01:47,900
- Who is it?
- Who's your crush?

43
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:50,833
- Just between us, okay?
- [TETAY] Just tell us!

44
00:01:50,833 --> 00:01:53,133
- Brent.
- Oh my God!

45
00:01:53,133 --> 00:01:54,400
- Brent Manalo?
- Yeah.

46
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:56,067
Hey, I know him!

47
00:01:56,067 --> 00:01:57,900
- Really?
- Yeah, he's Vince's friend.

48
00:01:57,900 --> 00:01:59,867
- Of course.
- You were with him on  PBB.

49
00:01:59,867 --> 00:02:01,167
Yeah, I know him really well.

50
00:02:01,167 --> 00:02:02,467
I was with him for two months.

51
00:02:02,467 --> 00:02:03,900
- Really?
- Yeah.

52
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:05,233
Why do you have a crush on him?

53
00:02:05,233 --> 00:02:06,533
Well, because, you know...

54
00:02:06,867 --> 00:02:07,967
You know how your crushes

55
00:02:07,967 --> 00:02:10,133
are always guys who definitely
wouldn't like you back?

56
00:02:10,133 --> 00:02:11,900
- Exactly!
- Wow!

57
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:14,033
It's already game over
at first sight.

58
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:16,367
Exactly. Even Empoy wouldn't
take a picture with you.

59
00:02:16,367 --> 00:02:19,100
- [LAUGHTER]
- Meme, you'll never know.

60
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:22,167
Exactly, you'll never know.
You'll never achieve.

61
00:02:22,167 --> 00:02:24,033
- Why...
- Mine's Emilio.

62
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:25,133
Emilio?

63
00:02:25,133 --> 00:02:26,300
- Yeah.
- Really?

64
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:27,567
- Yeah.
- But Emilio isn't here.

65
00:02:27,567 --> 00:02:29,567
Hacinto? No, I mean
the one from  PBB!

66
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:32,833
- Where is the hero here?
- I said the one from  PBB!

67
00:02:32,833 --> 00:02:34,533
We're talking about
<i> Call Me Mother!</i>

68
00:02:34,533 --> 00:02:37,633
Yeah, but Brent was with him
on  PBB.

69
00:02:37,633 --> 00:02:38,700
Oh my gosh!

70
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,200
Did you get close to Emilio?

71
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,067
- Yeah, he was my batchmate.
- Oh my God!

72
00:02:42,067 --> 00:02:43,500
Batchmates where?

73
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,833
I'm from La Salle,
he's from Ateneo.

74
00:02:45,833 --> 00:02:47,733
Oh, La Salle and Ateneo?
Fancy!

75
00:02:47,767 --> 00:02:49,633
Why are you into Emilio?

76
00:02:49,633 --> 00:02:50,867
He has this something...

77
00:02:50,867 --> 00:02:53,233
Like, if we met in person,
I feel like we'd really click.

78
00:02:53,233 --> 00:02:54,800
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

79
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:56,667
You know Emilio, right?

80
00:02:56,667 --> 00:02:58,733
Do you think Emilio
would like her?

81
00:02:58,733 --> 00:03:01,033
- It's possible.
- She could be his auntie.

82
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:03,300
- [LAUGHTER]
- Well... I talked to him.

83
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:05,133
He said he misses
his uncle in Saudi.

84
00:03:05,133 --> 00:03:08,300
Okay, I'm just going to eat
fish crackers!

85
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:11,033
- Maybe he'll like you.
- You never know! Come on!

86
00:03:11,033 --> 00:03:13,167
Who are you closer to,
Emilio or Brent?

87
00:03:13,167 --> 00:03:14,433
- Brent.
- [VERNA] Oh!

88
00:03:14,433 --> 00:03:16,533
We're both from La Salle.

89
00:03:16,533 --> 00:03:18,200
- Oh!
- That's why.

90
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,267
It runs in the blood.

91
00:03:19,267 --> 00:03:20,767
Do you have a problem
with Ateneo?

92
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,467
- Not really.
- [TETAY CHUCKLES]-

93
00:03:22,467 --> 00:03:24,200
Look at you with your
"that's why."

94
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,433
[LAUGHTER]

95
00:03:25,433 --> 00:03:29,067
Anyway, this is my
number one movie,

96
00:03:29,067 --> 00:03:30,900
<i>- Call Me Mother.
- Congratulations.</i>

97
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:32,633
- Congratulations.
- It's such a beautiful story.

98
00:03:32,633 --> 00:03:34,667
Yes. And it's even
more emotional

99
00:03:34,667 --> 00:03:36,667
when the theme song
starts playing.

100
00:03:36,667 --> 00:03:38,433
The<i>  Tala</i>  version
by Bryan Chong?

101
00:03:38,433 --> 00:03:40,333
Oh!

102
00:03:40,333 --> 00:03:42,900
It's nice because
they were fresh out of<i> PBB</i> then.

103
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:44,733
They starred in a movie.
It was Brent

104
00:03:44,733 --> 00:03:47,700
together with River.

105
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:48,700
- Yes.
- Yes.

106
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:50,667
He was Nadine Lustre's
husband there.

107
00:03:50,667 --> 00:03:52,500
And him too.
They've done a lot of projects.

108
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:53,933
Was it nice being in  PBB?

109
00:03:53,967 --> 00:03:54,967
Very.

110
00:03:54,967 --> 00:03:57,133
What's your most memorable
experience in  PBB?

111
00:03:57,133 --> 00:04:00,900
Maybe the free air conditioning
and food.

112
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:02,300
We're trying to save money
nowadays, right?

113
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:04,267
How many months were you
inside the<i>  PBB </i> house?

114
00:04:04,267 --> 00:04:05,667
I was there
for two months, Meme.

115
00:04:05,667 --> 00:04:07,933
- Oh, really.
- You got evicted right away.

116
00:04:07,933 --> 00:04:08,967
- Wow.
- I'm sorry, okay?

117
00:04:08,967 --> 00:04:09,967
[LAUGHTER]

118
00:04:09,967 --> 00:04:11,233
Her words sting, don't they?

119
00:04:11,233 --> 00:04:13,967
- Right!
- Your words sting.

120
00:04:13,967 --> 00:04:16,500
I want to know,
was it really hard

121
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:18,733
during your
first few weeks there?

122
00:04:18,733 --> 00:04:20,867
Yes, very. And I came there
a few weeks later.

123
00:04:20,867 --> 00:04:22,600
I needed to catch up
with all of them.

124
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:24,467
He was late
and not wearing his ID.

125
00:04:24,467 --> 00:04:25,900
- He was unable to get in.
- [LAUGHTER]

126
00:04:25,900 --> 00:04:28,267
Why did you come in later on?
Why not from the beginning?

127
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:30,467
That's what they wanted.

128
00:04:30,467 --> 00:04:32,567
Yes, I remember that.

129
00:04:32,567 --> 00:04:35,833
Say "I remember" again
and I'll punch you in the face.

130
00:04:35,833 --> 00:04:37,433
Yeah. This is the first time
we've heard

131
00:04:37,433 --> 00:04:38,767
a threadfin bream
speak in English.

132
00:04:38,767 --> 00:04:40,367
[SILLY SFX PLAYING]

133
00:04:40,367 --> 00:04:41,933
Is it your dream to be in  PBB?

134
00:04:41,933 --> 00:04:43,200
I actually auditioned

135
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,700
for the first celebrity
edition of  PBB.

136
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:46,700
- [TETAY] Okay.
- Ahh.

137
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:48,467
But I didn't get in.

138
00:04:48,467 --> 00:04:50,333
- [TETAY] I don't think I can.
- Why?

139
00:04:50,333 --> 00:04:52,233
Because you'd be away
for so long.

140
00:04:52,233 --> 00:04:53,533
I mean, for months.

141
00:04:53,533 --> 00:04:55,400
Why? Who would you miss
in the outside world?

142
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,867
I mean, of course,

143
00:04:56,867 --> 00:05:00,100
my family, my husband,
my kids, so...

144
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:02,867
- [VERNA] Aw!
- Right? [LAUGHS]

145
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:04,333
Husband, huh? [CHUCKLES]

146
00:05:04,333 --> 00:05:05,933
No, because I can't be--

147
00:05:05,933 --> 00:05:08,867
I can't afford to be away
from them even just for a week.

148
00:05:08,867 --> 00:05:10,100
I'd miss them badly.

149
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:12,233
- You'd really miss them.
- Yes. Absolutely--

150
00:05:12,233 --> 00:05:15,367
But what if ABS-CBN
or GMA tells you,

151
00:05:15,367 --> 00:05:19,200
"You won't be inside the house,
we'll just use your voice."

152
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:20,400
What if they do that.

153
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:21,867
But as a Kris Aquino
impersonator.

154
00:05:21,867 --> 00:05:23,033
- Huh?
- Ah, okay.

155
00:05:23,767 --> 00:05:24,900
[IN RESTRAINED VOICE]
Housemates,

156
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:28,000
please proceed
to the confession room.

157
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,033
[LAUGHTER]

158
00:05:29,033 --> 00:05:31,900
I have something to tell you.
Hurry up. [LAUGHS]

159
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:33,800
How about Verna being evicted.

160
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,400
- Verna.
- Yes, Auntie?

161
00:05:35,433 --> 00:05:37,233
Go to the confession room.

162
00:05:37,233 --> 00:05:38,467
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

163
00:05:38,467 --> 00:05:42,100
- Why?
- I saw the pork chop

164
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:43,233
in the kitchen.

165
00:05:43,233 --> 00:05:45,267
You ate it raw.

166
00:05:45,267 --> 00:05:46,267
[LAUGHTER]

167
00:05:46,267 --> 00:05:48,600
Verna, you need
to cook it first.

168
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:50,833
- It's fine, it was marinated.
- Wow!

169
00:05:50,833 --> 00:05:52,200
Wow!

170
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,933
She's so sassy. Marinated, huh?

171
00:05:53,933 --> 00:05:55,600
That's what I like about Verna.

172
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:57,800
She's very "I don't care,
I'll speak in English."

173
00:05:57,800 --> 00:06:00,300
- Because she feels like it.
- Confidence.

174
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:02,100
I don't eat raw.

175
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:04,367
Can you check
if the beef is tender?

176
00:06:04,367 --> 00:06:06,233
[LAUGHTER]

177
00:06:06,233 --> 00:06:07,800
- She speaks English well.
- True.

178
00:06:07,833 --> 00:06:09,200
Foreigners are attracted to her.

179
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:10,200
- [LAUGHTER]
- Hmm...

180
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,233
Yes.

181
00:06:11,233 --> 00:06:13,400
- Do you like foreigners?
- Are you a halfie?

182
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:17,067
- I can be.
- But are you really mixed,

183
00:06:17,067 --> 00:06:18,500
or are you pure Filipino?

184
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:20,900
I think Papa was a fourth,
and Mama too.

185
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,600
- Chinese and Spanish.
- Your papa's only a fourth,

186
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:24,400
and your Mama too, so
your family is just half then?

187
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:25,700
- [LAUGHTER]
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

188
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:28,167
- That's funny!
- Like a lengthwise pad.

189
00:06:28,167 --> 00:06:29,933
He's a looker
but not so good at math.

190
00:06:29,933 --> 00:06:33,133
His family is just a fourth,
so combined, that's just half.

191
00:06:33,133 --> 00:06:34,800
Are you guys still looking
for the other half?

192
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:36,367
He's not so good at fractions.

193
00:06:36,367 --> 00:06:38,900
- [APPLAUSE, CHEERING]
- Whoa!

194
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:42,933
- Hey! Hey!
- [LAUGHTER]

195
00:06:42,967 --> 00:06:45,300
She really is sassy!
"He's not so good at fractions."

196
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:48,433
What are the qualifications
in <i> PBB </i> for people to get in?

197
00:06:48,433 --> 00:06:50,733
- To be honest--
- You've got to have a backer?

198
00:06:50,733 --> 00:06:53,033
[CHUCKLES] Not really.

199
00:06:53,033 --> 00:06:55,933
You just have to be honest,
especially during auditions.

200
00:06:55,933 --> 00:06:58,700
You have to be genuine
with your intentions.

201
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:01,267
You have to have
a story to tell.

202
00:07:01,267 --> 00:07:03,167
- [VICE] Ahh.
- She has a lot.

203
00:07:03,167 --> 00:07:05,400
Stories that will inspire
Filipinos.

204
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:06,700
- Yes.
- She does.

205
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:09,233
- I inspire people.
- Yes.

206
00:07:09,233 --> 00:07:10,933
Especially those
who look like me.

207
00:07:10,933 --> 00:07:12,833
- [LAUGHTER]
- [TETAY] Hold on, that's an--

208
00:07:12,833 --> 00:07:15,133
- No one else looks like you.
- [LAUGHTER]

209
00:07:15,167 --> 00:07:16,567
You're the only one
in this world.

210
00:07:16,567 --> 00:07:18,000
I can point out some
in the audience.

211
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,433
[LAUGHTER]

212
00:07:19,433 --> 00:07:21,400
- Hey, they're our neighbors!
- I forgot.

213
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:23,167
Do you have plans to audition?

214
00:07:23,167 --> 00:07:24,233
I think I can.

215
00:07:24,233 --> 00:07:27,833
But I'm a hoarder when it comes
to online shopping.

216
00:07:27,833 --> 00:07:30,700
- What?
- I'm a parcel... hoarder.

217
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,467
What does that have
to do with  PBB?

218
00:07:32,467 --> 00:07:33,633
[TETAY] She won't be able
o receive it.

219
00:07:33,633 --> 00:07:35,500
Yeah. I don't want Big Brother
to receive it for me.

220
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:36,600
It's always cash on delivery.

221
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:39,867
- [LAUGHTER]
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

222
00:07:39,867 --> 00:07:41,833
She wants to be in <i> PBB
</i>but she's worried

223
00:07:41,833 --> 00:07:44,600
about her orders being
delivered while she's away.

224
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:45,967
She won't be able to receive it.

225
00:07:45,967 --> 00:07:47,433
How about you?

226
00:07:47,433 --> 00:07:49,433
If you audition,
do you think you'd get in?

227
00:07:49,467 --> 00:07:51,733
What will be your role
in the Big Brother house?

228
00:07:51,733 --> 00:07:54,400
Maybe I'll help with
the cleaning and organizing.

229
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:56,433
Stuff like that.
A sort of mother hen.

230
00:07:56,433 --> 00:07:58,133
- [VICE] Tetay has OCD.
- Not really.

231
00:07:58,133 --> 00:08:01,267
But I'm mad
about those crumbles.

232
00:08:01,267 --> 00:08:02,733
Stuff like that.

233
00:08:02,733 --> 00:08:04,433
I feel like I'd get in.

234
00:08:04,433 --> 00:08:06,033
- [VICE] Really?
- But...

235
00:08:06,033 --> 00:08:07,600
I think, I'm-- How about you?

236
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:08,567
- [VICE] What?
- Do you--

237
00:08:08,567 --> 00:08:09,567
No thanks.
I might get into a fight there.

238
00:08:09,567 --> 00:08:11,067
I might even curse Big Brother.

239
00:08:11,067 --> 00:08:12,000
- Hey!
-That's all I'm going to say.

240
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,167
I'm annoyed at him.

241
00:08:13,167 --> 00:08:14,533
He doesn't show his face
yet gives you tons of tasks.

242
00:08:14,533 --> 00:08:15,767
I don't even know him.

243
00:08:15,767 --> 00:08:17,333
- You were inside, right?
- Yes.

244
00:08:17,333 --> 00:08:18,433
